[Music]  okay  [Music]  i'm just heading out on a little morning  walk i try to do this every day  i do a morning walk and then a walking  tattoo  and it's just a nice way to like start  the day got my coffee  and trying not to eat my hair because  it's kind of windy out  look at these clouds so interesting  [Music]  these right here they look so pretty  right they almost look fuzzy but they're  so dangerous  i've gotten them stuck down in my leg  and on my foot and in my shoe and yeah  if you ever come across these pay  attention  [Music]  so  [Music]  [Music]  so  [Music]  so  [Music]  welcome to the desert welcome to my  office  so uh today is a work day i need to  answer emails and catch up on socials  um upload a few things and do some  financial stuff the main thing i want to  talk about today  is internet some of you have asked how  do you get internet in the van  it's pretty simple i just use my phone  to hotspot my laptop  so i use verizon and i have an unlimited  data  talk and text plan and it's about 90 a  month  and i believe it includes 30 gigabytes  of hotspot  so i've only run out once i figured out  why  is because i accidentally had my  creative cloud um  automatically updating whenever i would  connect to my hotspot and that drained  it one time  otherwise i find that i have more than  enough to like stream netflix  um upload even to youtube although i've  only done that a few times  and do everything social media and email  related when i moved into the van  i found i had way worse service it might  be the metal or the insulation or  something like that places where i used  to get four bars in my suv  i'd suddenly have one or two in the van  so i recently  installed a weboost drive range cell  booster  it has an outdoor antenna that picks up  a signal and sends it to the interior  antenna which then broadcasts to my  phone  the installation was pretty easy i wound  up routing the wire  under the weather ceiling in the back  door and down into the bench where the  box lives  and then connecting to the interior  antenna where i can easily plug and  unplug the box when i need it the bench  cushions hide the wires and i can still  get inside the bench to make my bed  easily i may end up doing a more  permanent installation down the road but  this works for now  okay so you can see here i have just one  bar of lte  and then i just have to plug in the dc  charger so now you can see i have three  bars  oh four bars even better another thing i  like to do when i roll up to a new  location  is test the internet speed using this  app called speed test  it will tell you just how much your  upload and download speed is  so you that's pretty high that's  more than enough to get most of my work  done another option is to purchase a  wi-fi device from your carrier and load  it with a certain amount of  internet my only experience with this is  when i was living  or traveling overseas and it worked  pretty great here in the states i just  use my phone because  your phone essentially works as a  hotspot so you actually need service in  order for the wi-fi device to work so  it's kind of the same thing  at least that's my understanding so  aside from my hotspot and signal booster  um i usually pop into libraries and  coffee shops  so i did that way more before covid  obviously hopefully things will get back  to normal soon  you can find really great wi-fi options  like whole foods  starbucks mcdonald's most cafes even  visitor centers  i hope those pointers were helpful i  have to get back to work  i have to update my budget and travel  expenses i haven't done that in a really  long time  so yay really exciting afternoon  you are my favorite place to go  you're  [Music]  one thing i love about living on the  road is  opening the door and being instantly  outside  [Music]  stones  i love the ground  [Music]  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

